 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "AVL and red-black trees are built for main memory. Databases and file systems keep their data on disk, where each access costs a million times more and moves a whole block. The B-tree is designed for that: wide and very short. This video builds one."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "B-trees"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the eight stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why disks need wide trees, the rules, how short a B-tree is, and searching."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then splitting full nodes, a sequence of insertions, deletion in outline, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=7]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: main memory answers in about 100 nanoseconds. A disk takes from a tenth of a millisecond to ten milliseconds."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: why wide trees"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And a disk always transfers a whole block, typically 4 to 16 kilobytes, even if you want one key."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So what matters is the number of blocks read, and each block should be packed with useful keys."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A balanced binary tree of a billion keys is about 30 levels deep: 30 disk reads per search. A B-tree with a thousand keys per node needs 3."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[3..=4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "count disk reads, not comparisons"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rules",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: Cormen describes a B-tree by its minimum degree t, at least 2. Every node except the root holds between t minus 1 and 2t minus 1 keys."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: the rules"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ru"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ru[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The root may hold as few as 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ru[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A node with k keys has k plus 1 children, and its keys, in sorted order, separate the key ranges of those children."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ru[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "All leaves are at the same depth: the tree is perfectly balanced in height."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ru[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With t equal to 2, nodes hold 1 to 3 keys: this is the 2-3-4 tree. Some books instead give the order m, the most children a node may have; then m is 2t."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ru[4..=5]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "t − 1 to 2t − 1 keys per node · leaves level"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "height",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: how tall can it be? The sparsest tree of height h has 1 key in the root, then 2 nodes, then 2t, then 2t squared, each with only t minus 1 keys."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 8: how short a B-tree is"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ru"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "hb"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Adding them up, n is at least 2 t to the h, minus 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "hb[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the height is at most log base t of n plus 1 over 2. The base is t, not 2: a much smaller number."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "hb[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With 1001 children per node, a tree of height 2 holds about a billion keys."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "hb[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Keep the root in memory, and any of a billion keys is found with 2 disk reads."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "hb[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "h ≤ log_t((n + 1)/2)"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "search",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: searching generalises the BST. In a node, scan its keys for the first one at least k."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 8: searching"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "hb"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "sc"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sc[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "If it equals k, done. If the node is a leaf, k is not in the tree."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sc[1..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Otherwise read the child that lies between the two neighbouring keys, and repeat there."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sc[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "One disk read per level: O of h reads, and O of t h comparisons in memory, which are almost free in comparison."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sc[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "one block per level"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "split",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: a node is full when it holds 2t minus 1 keys: with t equal to 2, three keys, like 10, 20, 30."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 5 of 8: splitting a full node"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "sc"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "sp"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Splitting it moves the median key, 20, up into the parent; 10 stays in one node, and 30 goes into a new node beside it."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sp[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Cormen splits proactively: on the way down, any full node is split before we enter it. So whenever a key moves up, the parent is guaranteed to have room, and one pass down is enough."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sp[3..=4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A B-tree grows taller only when the root splits. It grows at the top, not at the leaves, which is why all leaves stay at one depth."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sp[5]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "full node: median up, halves apart"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ins",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 6: insert 10 to 90 in steps of 10, with t equal to 2. 10, 20 and 30 fill the root."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 6 of 8: inserting 10 to 90"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "sp"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "s2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Insert 40. The root is full, so it is split first: 20 becomes a new root, with 10 and 30 below it. Then 40 joins 30."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "s2"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "s3"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "s3.b0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "50 joins 30 and 40, filling that leaf. Insert 60: on the way down, the full leaf 30, 40, 50 is split. 40 moves up beside 20, and 60 joins 50."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "s3"
